# Constraint set: the packages whose version can move a metric value, pinned to the RESULTS
# environment (env/results-v1.0.0.lock). Applied when compiling the Python 3.12 CI lock so that
# leg exercises exactly the numerics the published results and the manuscript report, instead of
# whatever floats resolve to on the day CI runs.
#
# The 3.10 leg is deliberately NOT constrained: these versions predate/postdate 3.10 support in
# ways that make the set unsolvable there, and its job is to prove the package still imports and
# passes on the oldest supported interpreter — not to reproduce numbers.
#
# Regenerate the pins from the captured env, do not hand-edit.
numpy==2.4.6
pandas==3.0.3
